    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-69973",
    ":question/problem": "Given that $B=2I$, where $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, what is the value of $det(B)?$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2I & =2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a diagonal matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
