    ":question/id": "b60c1c0e-c8ec-5aea-b1f6-7ec70c514424",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130235",
    ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices $A$ and $B$ given below. Find $\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}({B}^{T}).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1)=12 \\\\ det(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}=3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det({A}^{T}) & =det(A)=12 \\\\ det({B}^{T}) & =det(B)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{T})+det({B}^{T})=12+12=24.\n$$"
  },
