    ":question/id": "0cc67c3c-0334-59e3-b6fd-5c5b12713dd9",
    ":question/problem": "Find the determinant of the matrix\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0.5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & \\pi \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "All entries below the main diagonal are zero, so $T$ is upper triangular. Its determinant is the product of its main diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\det(T)=2\\cdot(-1)\\cdot3\\cdot2=-12.\n$$\n\nThe off-diagonal entries do not enter this product."
